        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "dd19609a-ab09-50b9-bcb6-222d5651a94a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Mark Evans, Bon Scott\n- Bands: AC/DC, Rose Tattoo\n- Albums: T.N.T., High Voltage, Dirty Deeds Done Dirt Cheap, Let There Be Rock, '74 Jailbreak\n- Works: Dirty Deeds: My Life Inside/Outside of AC/DC\n- Topics: album releases, band membership\n\nFacts:\n- Mark Whitmore Evans was born on 2 March 1956 and is an Australian bass guitarist.\n- Mark Evans was an early member of AC/DC from March 1975 to June 1977.\n- Mark Evans later became the bass guitarist for the Australian rock band Rose Tattoo.\n- Mark Evans' playing appeared on AC/DC's albums T.N.T., High Voltage, Dirty Deeds Done Dirt Cheap, Let There Be Rock, and '74 Jailbreak.\n- Dirty Deeds Done Dirt Cheap is an album by the Australian hard rock band AC/DC.\n- Dirty Deeds Done Dirt Cheap was AC/DC's third LP and was released in Australia and Europe in 1976.\n- Dirty Deeds Done Dirt Cheap was not released in the United States until 1981, more than one year after Bon Scott's death.\n- Mark Evans' autobiography, Dirty Deeds: My Life Inside/Outside of AC/DC, was released in December 2011.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "7b75c887-5ec9-5de7-a5cb-63a98097a49e",
        "text": "Page: Mark Evans (musician). Sentence: Mark Whitmore Evans (born 2 March 1956) is an Australian bass guitarist for the Australian rock band Rose Tattoo who was an early member of hard rock band AC/DC from March 1975 to June 1977.\nPage: Mark Evans (musician). Sentence: His playing featured on their albums \"T.N.T\", \"High Voltage\", \"Dirty Deeds Done Dirt Cheap\", \"Let There Be Rock\" and \"'74 Jailbreak\".\nPage: Mark Evans (musician). Sentence: Evans' autobiography, \"Dirty Deeds: My Life Inside/Outside of AC/DC\" was released in December 2011.\nPage: Dirty Deeds Done Dirt Cheap. Sentence: Dirty Deeds Done Dirt Cheap is an album by Australian hard rock band AC/DC.\nPage: Dirty Deeds Done Dirt Cheap. Sentence: It was the band's third LP released in Australia and in Europe in 1976 but was not released in the US until 1981, more than one year after Bon Scott's death.",
